0	section	Gardener 5
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Are you a member of the Group of Advanced Gardeners?
2	line	Player	Are you a member of the Group of Advanced Gardeners?
2	line	[Gardener #5]	Why, yes I am. Why do you ask?
2	line	Player	Martin has asked me to investigate why all the crops are failing.
2	line	[Gardener #5]	Well I can tell by the look on your face that I'm not the first person you've asked. Why don't you tell me what you've heard from other members of the group so far?
2	line	Player	Why not? They all seem to be a bunch of loonies anyway.
2	line	Player	I've been told that it's the lack of rain, plagues of insects and recently I was told that the entire order of seasons is confused!
2	line	Player	I have no idea what to do about any of it. I'm an adventurer, not a weather controller!
2	line	[Gardener #5]	Did you ever consider that all those theories might be correct?
2	line	Player	But they're all different, how could they all be correct?
2	line	[Gardener #5]	I'll let you into a little secret that'll explain it all to you. In a word - fairies!
2	line	Player	Oh no! Not another crack-pot theory!
2	line	[Gardener #5]	I'm serious!
2	line	[Gardener #5]	Think it through. There are fairies who control everything natural from the weather to the seasons.
2	line	[Gardener #5]	Surely if all of those things have been mentioned as catalysts to our problems it stands to reason that the fairies are actually the cause?
2	line	Player	Right, well thanks for your input. I'll think over what you said.
2	action	end
