0	section	Returning to Martin
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Ask about the Skillcape of Farming.
1	option	Ask about the quest.
2	line	Martin the Master Gardener	Hello again, {player}. How are you getting on with solving the Gardening Group's problems?
2	line	Player	To be honest I'm worried about the sort of person you let join your organisation.
2	line	Martin the Master Gardener	Why is that?
2	line	Player	I've heard theories ranging from climate change to fairies from your members.
2	line	Martin the Master Gardener	Hmm, that's an interesting idea. Now that I think about it that does make some sense. Yes, maybe you should talk to a fairy about it.
2	line	Player	O-kay! You're the boss, any idea which flower I should look under to find a fairy?
2	line	Martin the Master Gardener	No, sorry, but I did hear that there were some adventurers with a similar problem in the swamps near Lumbridge. Just don't mention my name if you talk to them, they're trying to keep it a secret, but everybody actually knows what they're up to.
2	line	Player	Yes, I've spoken to them before.
2	action	end
0	section	Entering Zanaris
0	section	Talking to the Fairy Godfather
1	line	Player	Who are you? Where's the Fairy Queen? What's going on here? Where's the Fairy Queen's throne gone?
1	line	Fairy Godfather	Ciao esploratore! So many questions. Whicha one would you hava me answer first?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Who are you?
2	line	Player	Who are you?
2	line	Fairy Godfather	Me?! I am-a da Fairy Godfather.
2	line	Player	...?
2	line	Fairy Godfather	I see-a by your face dat you have-a not-a heard of-a me. Irrispettoso, eet iz of no eemportance. You weesh-a to know sometheeng else or no?
2	action	other
1	option	Where's the Fairy Queen?
2	line	Player	Where's the Fairy Queen?
2	line	Fairy Godfather	Ah, eet iz a trageec-a tale. Da Queen Bee she iz-a, how-you-say, seek?
2	line	Player	You mean sick. What happened?
2	line	Fairy Godfather	Ah, a tragedy to be-a struck-a down so young.
2	line	Fairy Godfather	How-a much do ya know about-a da fairy folk, my beeg friend?
2	line	Player	Not actually a whole deal, I'm afraid.
2	line	Fairy Godfather	Well, let-a me enlighten yous. Zanaris iz-a a nexus of-a da worlds. Da Queen Bee, she iz-a da guardian of-a all da folk dat live-a in Zanaris.
2	line	Fairy Godfather	So when-a thees Tanglefoot arrives, da Queen Bee she-a goes to da Cosmic Temple area to kill-a eet, but someting goes-a wrong. Da Queen Bee, she gets-a hurt and is-a now inna da magic sleep.
2	line	Fairy Godfather	She is-a being cared for by-a Fairy Nuff, who lives-a just north of-a da bank.
2	line	Player	Thanks, I'll go see her then. Goodbye.
2	line	Fairy Godfather	Ciao. Oh, and {player}...
2	line	Player	Yes?
2	line	Fairy Godfather	A word-a of advice. You be-a careful not to cause da trouble for da folk while you are in Zanaris. Ciao.
2	line	Player	?
2	action	end
1	option	What's going on here?
2	line	Player	What's going on here?
2	line	Fairy Godfather	Hmm, an eenteresting question, my friend. I am-a trying to run-a da fairy kingdom, and youz iz-a being da irritating adventurer.
2	line	Player	That's not what I mean!
2	line	Fairy Godfather	No, but-a dat iz da question I answered. Now iz-a dere anything else?
2	action	other
1	option	Where's the Fairy Queen's throne gone?
2	line	Player	Where's the Fairy Queen's throne gone?
2	line	Fairy Godfather	An eenteresting place to start... I am-a here, ze Queen Bee iz not. So my chair - eet iz-a here, her throne - eet iz-a not. Eez there anytheeng else? I ama a bizy fairy.
2	action	other
1	option	That's all, thanks.
2	line	Player	That's all, thanks.
2	line	Fairy Godfather	Eef there iz anytheeng I can-a help you weeth whilst you are-a veesiting Zanaris, plsi, do not-a trouble to bother me.
2	action	end
0	section	Trying to talk to the Fairy Godfather again
1	line	Fat Rocco	Da Boss is a busy fairy! He don' have time to talk to yous humans. Vamoose!
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Fairy Nuff
1	line	Fairy Nuff	Sorry, I'm very busy and can't chat. If you want to know something go and talk to the Godfather.
1	line	Player	I did, he said I should come and talk to you!
1	line	Fairy Nuff	Oh!
1	line	Fairy Nuff	Sorry, I didn't realise.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	What can I help you with then?
1	line	Player	Actually it's more a case of what can I help you with? I told the Fairy Godfather that I would help you find a cure for the Queen.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	Oh, thank you! I really need help, I have no idea what ails the Queen. You must be a mighty healer!
1	line	Player	Err...no, not me.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	A great druid then?
1	line	Player	Umm...'fraid not.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	A shaman?
1	line	Player	No.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	A surgeon?
1	line	Player	No.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	A doctor, medic, nurse?
1	line	Player	No, no and no.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	So what are you then?
1	line	Player	I'm a mighty adventurer!
1	line	Fairy Nuff	A what?!
1	line	Player	A mighty adventurer!
1	line	Fairy Nuff	Yes, I heard. It's just not what I was expecting to hear.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	But hang on, you might be just the sort of person I need to help me!
1	line	Player	How is that then?
1	line	Fairy Nuff	I'm sure the Godfather told you that the Queen is in an enchanted sleep?
1	line	Player	Well sort of, I couldn't really understand everything he was talking about.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	Shhh, somebody might hear. Look you're a visitor, so I'll tell you this much; it doesn't pay to talk about the Godfather behind his back.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	But back to the problem at hand - the Fairy Queen. She was brought here after her battle with the Tanglefoot in a terrible state, extremely weak and barely able to fly!
1	line	Fairy Nuff	Here, I've written down a list of her symptoms.
1	action	
1	line	Fairy Nuff	When the Queen got back here, she was clearly weakening fast. It appears as if the magic force that is her life essence is slowly unravelling.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	I have put her in a state of tempus fugit, that will slow time down for her, and thus prolong the amount of time that she remains alive.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	Now, what I need you to do is find a mage by the name of Zandar Horfyre. He has spent many years studying magical illness. Take the list to him and ask him if he knows what ails the Queen, please.
1	line	Player	That doesn't sound too difficult, where will I find him.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	I believe he now resides in the Dark Wizards' tower near Falador, and {player}, please hurry. I fear the Queen doesn't have much time left!
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Fairy Nuff again
1	line	Fairy Nuff	You're back soon! Did you find out what ails the Fairy Queen?
1	line	Player	No, I'm afraid I've lost the list of symptoms you gave me.
1	line	Fairy Nuff	Well not to worry, I have a copy of it here.
1	action	end
0	section	At the Dark Wizard's Tower
0	section	Talking to Zandar Horfyre
1	line	Player	Hello, I need your help.
1	line	Zandar Horfyre	And why should I help you, fool? You attack my brethren and I, and then you demand my help! I think not!
1	line	Player	But Fairy Nuff said you would help me!
1	line	Zandar Horfyre	Fairy Nuff sent you!
1	line	Zandar Horfyre	How is she? I owe her a great deal, she saved me from a mortal injury I sustained when I was investigating the nature of Otherworldly beings. So, how can I help?
1	line	Player	The Fairy Queen is extremely ill. She was in a battle with a Tanglefoot and her injuries have resulted in her being in a coma.
1	line	Zandar Horfyre	This is grave news indeed!
1	line	Zandar Horfyre	You think the Tanglefoot is responsible? I don't see how that could be. A Tanglefoot will normally kill its victim outright...unless...hmmm...I wonder...
1	line	Zandar Horfyre	I don't suppose you could give me more details about the Fairy Queen's condition, could you?
1	cond	If the player has the symptoms list:
2	line	Player	Fairy Nuff gave me a list of her symptoms. Here, have a look at it.
2	line	Zandar Horfyre	Hmm...yes...slow discorporation of ethereal body, eh? Hmm...I think I know what the problem might be.
2	line	Player	You do? That's great! What is it?
2	line	Zandar Horfyre	From what I know about fairies, their basic lifeforce is pure magic. Much as we humans would refer to our souls as our life essence, so too does a fairy have a life essence of pure magic.
2	line	Zandar Horfyre	You could actually refer to fairies as magic embodied and not be wrong.
2	line	Player	Yes, but about the Fairy Queen?
2	line	Zandar Horfyre	Patience, I'm getting to that. It appears the Fairy Queen has lost a large part, indeed the majority, of her life essence. Either it was drained from her by the Tanglefoot or she did it voluntarily.
2	line	Zandar Horfyre	Although why she would do that is beyond me.
2	line	Player	So I guess I need to go and kill this Tanglefoot and get back her magic essence if I am to help her?
2	action	The symptoms list is taken.
2	line	Zandar Horfyre	Yes, but if I were you I would seek Malignus Mortifer, the necromancer. He's been seen near Port Sarim with his followers recently. I believe he once fought a Tanglefoot.
2	line	Player	Malignus Mortifer. Okay, thanks very much.
2	line	Zandar Horfyre	Don't mention it, and give my regards to Nuff, when you see her next.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player doesn't have the symptoms list:
2	line	Player	Fairy Nuff gave me a list of her symptoms, but I don't have it with me.
2	line	Zandar Horfyre	Well, I can't diagnose the problem without knowing the symptoms. You'd better go and find that list, or get Fairy Nuff to give you another one.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Malignius Mortifer
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Who are you and what are you doing here?
1	option	I need help with fighting a Tanglefoot.
2	line	Player	I need help with fighting a Tanglefoot. Can you help me?
2	line	Malignius Mortifer	Almost certainly, I am a great practitioner of the magic arts, after all.
2	line	Player	Great, thanks. I was told by Zandar Horfyre that you fought one once.
2	line	Malignius Mortifer	That is true and an epic battle it was too.
2	line	Player	That's great! I presume you won as you are here to tell me about it, could you tell me how to defeat one, please?
2	line	Malignius Mortifer	Of course I won! As I've already stated I am a master of the magic arts.
2	line	Malignius Mortifer	Why do you want to know how to kill a Tanglefoot?
2	line	Player	There is a Tanglefoot in the lost city of Zanaris and I have been asked to kill it.
2	line	Malignius Mortifer	I see. Well I could tell you how to defeat your Tanglefoot, however I would need you to perform a little undertaking for me first.
2	line	Player	What exactly did you have in mind?
2	line	Malignius Mortifer	To the north-east of here is a haunted manor. Bring me a skull from a grave you find there and you shall have your answer.
2	cond	If the player already has the skull in their inventory:
3	line	Player	Actually I have it right here.
3	line	Malignius Mortifer	Excellent, hand it over then.
3	line	Malignius Mortifer	Right then, to business. A Tanglefoot can not be harmed by might nor magic. The only weapon that can damage them are a pair of enchanted secateurs!
3	line	Player	Where can I get a pair of these enchanted secateurs?
3	line	Malignius Mortifer	You will have to make them... listen carefully and I'll tell you how.
3	line	Malignius Mortifer	Obviously you will need a pair of secateurs, you will also need to gather [item 1], [item 2] and [item 3].The three items are consecutive entries of the list, e.g. "an uncut ruby, some Jogre bones and a kingworm".
3	line	Malignius Mortifer	Take them to the Nature Spirit and ask him to perform the ceremony of Phasma Phasmatis Natura.
3	line	Player	Phasma Phasmatis Natura. Got it! Is that all?
3	line	Malignius Mortifer	Yes, that's all. You'll be able to use those secateurs to kill the monster.
3	line	Player	Great, thanks very much.
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player does not have the skull in their inventory:
3	line	Player	I'll go and get it then.
3	line	Malignius Mortifer	Fine, I'll see you soon.
3	action	end
